# Build output.
/target/
**/target/

# LexLean build roots inside examples and fixture projects. The committed
# artifacts are the expected/ oracles, never a live build directory.
examples/**/.lexlean/
# Fetched Lean libraries and Lake build products of an example (SPEC.md §10.4).
examples/**/.lake/
demos/**/.lake/
demos/**/.lexlean/
tests/**/.lexlean/
compiler/.lexlean/

# The assembled release artifact set (§30.3). `cargo xtask release-artifacts`
# derives it, the release workflow attaches it, and it is output, never source:
# committing it would put a second copy of SPEC.md and the licenses in the tree
# and make `cargo package` read a dirty working directory.
/release/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# `Cargo.lock` is NOT ignored: the resolved version of every dependency is part
# of the claim made against it (R6).

# Claude Code worktrees and session state (never part of the release set).
.claude/
stdlib/.lexlean/
std-models/.lexlean/
std-reasoning/.lexlean/
bootstrap/.lexlean/
